G4715.definition:
στατήρ , -ῆρος, ὁ 
 [in Aq., Sm., for מִשְׁקָל ;] 
 a stater ; 
 __(a)  a weight ; 
 __(b)  a coin  (used by late writers of the Greek τετράδραχμον):  Mat.17:27 26:16 , WH, mg.†
 (AS)

G4733.definition:
στερέωμα , -τος, τό
 (στερεόω), [in LXX:  Gen.1:6  ff.,  Psa.19:1 150:1 ,  Eze.1:22-26 10:1 13:5 , Dan LXX, TH  Dan.3:56 ,  Dan.12:3  (רָקִיעַ),  Deu.33:26  (שַׁחַק),  Psa.18:2 71:3  (סֶלַע),  Est.9:29 , I  Est.8:78  (82),  Sir.43:1 , 8,  1Ma.9:14  * ;] 
 a solid body ; 
 __(a)  a support, foundation  (Arist., al.); metaphorically, strength ( Psa.17:1-15 70:1-5 , 1Mac, ll. with); steadfastness,  firmness : τ. πίστεως,  Col.2:5;  
 __(b) the dome of heaven (believed to be a solid canopy), the firmament (LXX).†
 (AS)

G4751.definition:
στόμαχος , -ου, ὁ
 (στόμα), 
prop., a mouth, an opening; 
 __(a) in early Gk. writers, the throat; 
 __(b)  of the opening of the stomach  (Arist.); 
 __(with) in later writers (Plut., al.),  the stomach :  1Ti.5:23. †
 (AS)
